# Terminal colour palettes for file listings and completion menus.
#
# LS_COLORS is read by GNU ls, by Zsh's completion menu through the
# list-colors zstyle in 40-completion.zsh, and by eza — which is why this file
# has to be sourced before completion is configured. LSCOLORS is the BSD
# equivalent that macOS ls reads.
#
# Kept in its own file because the palette is several hundred lines on its own
# and has nothing to do with the rest of the environment.

# Keep the legacy file-type colours for GNU ls and Zsh completion menus, split into a readable array.
typeset -a legacy_ls_colors

